From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michiel Bruijn <michiel@bruijn.nu>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:17:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Don't flush a window surface when its shape doesn't
 change.

Every SetWindowPos of a child updates the region of its toplevel's surface,
and window_surface_set_shape() flushed the surface even when the shape
stayed the same. A window that lays out its children showed every
intermediate step: resizing a TopSolid command panel showed the panel at
its new width with the controls still at the old one, and their old
pixels next to the new ones. Windows shows a WS_EX_COMPOSITED window only
once it is painted. Flush like EndPaint does instead, only when the
application doesn't go idle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHfFhG2yCUatEx7FMTfCMT
---
 dlls/win32u/dce.c    | 7 ++++++-
 dlls/win32u/window.c | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/dce.c b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
index 836156f1d21..2ce51a051a4 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/dce.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
@@ -712,6 +712,8 @@ void window_surface_set_clip( struct window_surface *surface, HRGN clip_region )
 
 void window_surface_set_shape( struct window_surface *surface, HRGN shape_region )
 {
+    BOOL changed = FALSE;
+
     window_surface_lock( surface );
 
     if (!shape_region && surface->shape_region)
@@ -719,17 +721,20 @@ void window_surface_set_shape( struct window_surface *surface, HRGN shape_region
         NtGdiDeleteObjectApp( surface->shape_region );
         surface->shape_region = 0;
         surface->bounds = surface->rect;
+        changed = TRUE;
     }
     else if (shape_region && !NtGdiEqualRgn( shape_region, surface->shape_region ))
     {
         if (!surface->shape_region) surface->shape_region = NtGdiCreateRectRgn( 0, 0, 0, 0 );
         NtGdiCombineRgn( surface->shape_region, shape_region, 0, RGN_COPY );
         surface->bounds = surface->rect;
+        changed = TRUE;
     }
 
     window_surface_unlock( surface );
 
-    window_surface_flush( surface );
+    /* an unchanged shape would show what is painted so far, like a half laid out window */
+    if (changed) window_surface_flush( surface );
 }
 
 /*******************************************************************
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
index f776e1191c9..8bb183503d9 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -2121,6 +2121,8 @@ static void update_surface_region( HWND hwnd )
 done:
     if (shape) NtGdiDeleteObjectApp( shape );
     release_win_ptr( win );
+    /* like EndPaint: only an application that doesn't go idle shows its windows while it moves them */
+    flush_window_surfaces( FALSE );
 }
 
 
